One not-so-obvious advantage of eXcursion is that your academic
institution has a campus software license grant (CSLG), you can buy
quantity-one media and then install it legally on all of your W/NT
systems.

Also, although an individual window is only 8-bit, you avoid the
color-flashing that occurs when you have an 8-bit frame buffer.

I use eXcursion all the time, both at home and at work (I migrated to
W/NT on the desk).

The primary changes I'd like to see would be better color management (i.e.,
>8 bit) and support for OpenGL using the W/NT OpenGL support.

