"eaml" <eaml@ix.netcom.com> wrote:
>
> Can anybody tell me if there is you can do PPP on VMS?
>
  Yes you can, but the solution is dependent on platform (VAX/Alpha) and the
  specific VMS version.

  Generally - VMS for Alpha (starting with a version which I dont remember at
  the moment) has PPP "built-in", and the system probably comes with a NAS
  license which permits the use of TCP/IP.

  VAXen, however, dont have PPP built-in (they, rather, have DDCMP). As UCX
  doesnt support PPP (AFAIK. I think it supports SLIP, though), you'll probably
  have to purchase a TCP/IP stack that does. I think MULTINET supports PPP.
>
> Maybe a free gnu perhaps
>
  Nope, but CMU-TEK is free, though I dont know if it supports PPP.

  BTW - dont crosspost so massively. Two or three newsgroups are always
  enough for this kind of questions - comp.os.vms, vmsnet.networks.tcp-ip.misc,
  and comp.sys.vms are more then sufficient for a start.

 Hope this helps,
                  Uri Raz.

